   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing political subdivisions to permit any public body to hold\nmeetings remotely and without in-person access during the COVID-19 state\ndisaster emergency; and provides for the repeal of such provisions upon the\nexpiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6303",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6303-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6303\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing political subdivisions to permit any public body to\nhold meetings remotely and without in-person access during the COVID-19\nstate disaster emergency; and provides for the repeal of such provisions\nupon the expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize political subdivisions to hold public meetings remotely\nwhile also ensuring such meetings are publicly available.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes political subdivisions to hold meetings remotely\nprovided that the public has the ability to view or listen to such\nproceeding and that such meetings are recorded and later transcribed.\n\nSection 2 provides for an immediate effective date, which will expire\npursuant to the expiration of Executive Order 202 of 2020.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe COVID-19 pandemic has restricted the ability of municipalities,\nschool districts and other special districts to hold public meetings and\nprotect public health. However, the need to conduct municipal business\nremains. Executive Order 202 of 2020 authorizes meetings to be conducted\nremotely while also providing guaranteed public access.  This legis-\nlation is intended to codify the provisions of the executive order and\nprovide greater certainty to local governments regarding the conduct of\ntheir public meetings.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall expire and be deemed\nrepealed on the same date as the same expiration of the state disaster\nemergency declared pursuant to executive order 202 of 2020.\n",
